11
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Dale, played by Scott Glenn.

12
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Greenland is a 2020 American apocalyptic survival disaster thriller film
directed by Ric Roman Waugh and written by Chris Sparling.

13
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
The film stars Gerard Butler (who also produced), Morena Baccarin, Roger Dale Floyd, Scott Glenn, David Denman, and Hope Davis, and follows a family who
must fight for survival as a planet-destroying comet races to Earth while the people around them get more and more desperate to survive.

14
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
Originally scheduled to be theatrically released in the United States,
Greenland was delayed several times due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

15
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film was released domestically by STXfilms, through video on demand on December
18, 2020, and then to streaming on HBO Max and Amazon Prime Video.

16
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
It was also released theatrically in other territories,
beginning with Belgium on July 29, 2020.

17
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
The film received generally positive reviews.

18
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
The film grossed $52.3 million worldwide with a
production budget of $35 million.

19
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
A sequel, Greenland 2: Migration, was released on January 9, 2026.

20
01:49:05,454 --> 01:49:11,454
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship,
panic, kidnapping, looting, natural disaster.

21
01:54:32,727 --> 01:54:38,727
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
